Hi everyone,

I've been logging my tournament game for a bit of fun, and luckily it's 
turned out to be a good one. As per Ellora the Elven Archer, I'm not 
really looking for hints or spoilers, just to tell my story of 
"Clockwise the Barbarian". Let me know if you enjoyed your reading.


Part I - start of the adventure!
-------------------------

I have decided to play the character that I have been trying to ascend 
for the past year - a male barbarian. (Yes, I just want to be Arnie). 
I've created my account on devnull, found a server (sahara) and logged 
in. It's all ASCII!! Arghgh! This is going to be taking some getting
used to! I've searched the newsgroups, turns out it isn't possible to 
use tiles at all. Oh well, tough. It'll be fun! I've turned on IBM 
graphics and color, and things seem ok.

On the first level I found some buckled boots. What would you do in that 
situation? Put them on of course! Doh, they were cursed and gave me -4 
to my AC!

Damn it, now I'm on 10 AC. Anyway. Cleared the first level, nothing to 
report. Found a scroll, in an act of madness decided to read it. Luckily 
I just teleported to a different room. Phew. No more of that risky 
business from now on!

Second level, found a staircase down to the gnome mines. Went down to 
the mines and explored in the dark. Killed 3 monsters and gained 2 
levels as a result :) Woohoo! Got surrounded by 3 monsters, got scared, 
got very scared, and decided to make a very quick retreat back upstairs!
He who lives to run away, lives to fight another day...


Explored the rest of level 2, found 2 altars (!!), but none were my 
alignment (neutral)! Oh well, that's cool. Down to level 3.

Level 3 - Found a shop!! Bought two brass lanterns, plus a key! Cool, 
very handy, now I can start exploring the mines properly with a light! 
Went back up to level 2, then down to the mines.


Day 2. Entry into Minetown.
-----------------------------

Went through the mines and managed to grab the luckstone. (Well I'm 
pretty sure it's a luckstone, I've only found 1 identify scroll so far.) 
No major drama's to report (got hissed at by a chickatrice but I think I 
got lucky). The altar in minetown was not my alignment so I haven't 
sacrificed anything. Hey maybe I could go back up to level 2 and try to 
convert an altar? I've got a bag of tricks.. might be the way to go. 
Good news is that I've managed to find 2 magic markers on the way - do I 
use them to write more identify scrolls? Decisions decisions! Also 
picked up some better armor so I've got an AC 0.

More good news, on level 5 I was immediately greeted by two demons, I 
think it was a water demon and a silver demon? (Can't remember now). 
Anyway, they were relatively easy to kill and then realised that I was 
on a bones level! Wohoo, a player named "Revlar" left me some goodies, 
nothing major though. I wonder how and why those demons were there? 
Maybe he drank from a fountain, I've heard that strange things can 
happen if you do that (I just stay away from drinking them). Looks like 
he got a bit too clever for his own boots... serves as a severe warning 
for me.

So I've ventured back to level 2 and I'm going to try to convert this 
Chaotic altar. I've got a bag of tricks and a wand of create monster. 
Here we go.. first sacrifice.. no luck! "Unluckily, you feel the power 
of Crom decrease".  Second sacrifice... alright! The altar glows gray 
and I'm in business! I sacrificed quite a bit but no Cleaver yet... 
that's cool, I can wait.

Ventured down to level 6, found and drank a potion.. "You feel a bit
strange.. You turn into a bone devel!".

What the hell???

Since when did a potion of polymorph ever exist?!!

Well, there you go, and there goes my mithril coat. Might have to 
venture back down into the mines and pick up the other one when I turn 
back. Well, for the moment I've got an AC of -3, so unless I can't do 
something neccesary I might as well stay this way for a while! That is, 
unless I attack people by biting them - I've done that before and bit 
into a chickatrice.. what a way to die.


Day 3.
-----------------------------

Ventured down pretty far into the dungeons of doom. I am now on level 
19. Lots has happened. I have the mighty Vorpal Blade which has been 
enchanted to +5 (I think), an AC of -4, and a few magic markers. 
Annoyingly enough I haven't found a lot of scrolls so I can't write much!

I found my quest level (13), but don't have anywhere near enough 
experience to start on it so I went back up. Also found sokoban but 
haven't started on it yet.

Today on level 18 I found a chickatrice nest! Yikes! Within the nest 
there were quite a few corpses; stabwound, iankeith, greycat, another 
greycat, anselmus1, another greycat and eit_brad. Quite a few people had 
fallen pray to the nasty chickatrices! Fortunately not me. There is also 
a nurse on that level but for some reason my armour is cursed, so I 
can't take it off to do a bit of nurse dancing. Oh well, no hurry for that.

On level 19 there is something strange.. a throne room with no monsters. 
Might be another bones file, not sure yet. Must be, I've found 
aardvark's ghost. Sat on the throne but no wish.. oh well. Also found 
another eit_brad corpse.

I think that it's about time I go back to my altar on level 8 and do a 
bit of praying. So I ventured my way up and dove straight into prayer. 
No point in wasting time. Crom was well pleased with me and granted me 
the gift of stealth! How nice! Plus he also removed the curse off my 
armour, and blessed my water potions. Fantastic.

So I've ventured back down to level 19, where I found some cursed silver 
dragon scales... hmmmm, I wonder if casting "enchant armour" on these 
will convert them to "proper armour" as well as removing the curse? I 
gave it a bash... and it did! I am now AC -6!

Next time I plan on venturing down to Medusa, then all the way back up 
to complete Sokoban and my quest. Things that I really want to find:

a genocide scroll
a bag of holding

well, that'll do for the moment, no need to get greedy.


